#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""Event daemon: watches herdr panes and pushes EVENT lines into the PM pane. Runs outside Claude Code.

  pm-watchd start [--pm <pane-id|agent-name>] [--interval 60] [--mem 22.5] [--cpu 90] [--ctx 300000] [--pm-ctx 400000] [--stale-hours 3]
  pm-watchd stop | status | tail [N] | whoami

Start it at the beginning of every PM session from the PM pane. The PM pane is found from the process tree (Claude)
or as the one working unregistered agent in this folder (Codex, whose shell commands run in an app-server with a
frozen HERDR_PANE_ID); `whoami` shows the result without starting. A running daemon is restarted so it follows this
PM pane and this PM session id; pm.json records them for pm-archive.

The daemon does not poll. It subscribes to herdr's event socket (a pane's agent status changed, a pane opened,
closed or exited) and is signalled by pm-report and pm-emulator-image when they append a line and by pm-check when a
run ends, so it looks the moment something happens. --interval is only the fallback: the longest it sleeps when nothing wakes it,
and the whole cadence while the socket is unreachable (logged once when that starts and once when it ends). What
happened is always judged from `herdr agent list` and the report files, never from the event itself.

Events, each delivered as one prompt line to the PM, or to the plan that leads the issue the line is about (issue 478,
_pmroute.py): a line about a worker, rev or crit pane of an issue, or about a worktree of it, goes to its live plan
`i<n>-plan`; everything else, and everything of an issue with no live plan, to the PM:
  EVENT ready <pane> <STAGE READY|UNIT READY|ISSUE READY|BLOCKED|DONE line> a registered pane finished a turn with a reporting line
  EVENT silent <pane>                                           a registered pane's turn ended with no typed line (pane-mode.md,
                                                                Reporting lines), at the moment herdr says its turn ended
  EVENT room <pane> pane <role> <side>                          to the pane a QUEUE answer of pm-pane told to wait: there is room now
  EVENT room <pane> check <checkout>                            to the pane a WAIT answer of pm-check told to wait: there is room
                                                                now (the longest waiting first, one per look). Room is judged only
                                                                when something frees it: a check ends, a pane closes or is gone,
                                                                the timer's reading of memory and CPU is under the limits, or the
                                                                token rate goes back under its target
  EVENT emulator-image refreshed <before> -> <after>           a refresh moved aws-emulator to a new version or commit (pm-emulator-image)
  EVENT emulator-image failed <reason>                        a refresh failed; aws-emulator was left as it was (pm-emulator-image)
  EVENT blocked <pane>                                          a pane waits at a permission/question dialog
  EVENT gone <pane>                                             a registered pane disappeared
  EVENT unregistered <pane> <pane id>                           herdr holds an agent named like a pane (i<n>-<role>[-<unit>]) in
                                                                this checkout or a worktree of it that the registry does not hold
                                                                in that pane, and no pm-pane opens or closes it now (issue 504);
                                                                judged on every look, which herdr's pane events and the end of a
                                                                pm-pane new or close bring; told once per pane
  EVENT stale <pane> <hours>                                    working with no state change for --stale-hours
  EVENT ctx <pane> <tokens>                                     a pane's context passed --ctx (again every +50K)
  EVENT ctx pm <tokens>                                         the PM's own context passed --pm-ctx
  EVENT mem <used>GB swap <used>/<total>GB top=<pane> <GB>,…    memory over --mem (at most once per 10 min)
  EVENT mem ok <used>GB                                         back under budget after a mem event (once)
  EVENT cpu <pct>% top=<pane> <GB>,…                            CPU over --cpu on three looks in a row, 30 s apart (at most once per 10 min)
  EVENT cpu ok <pct>%                                           back under after a cpu event (once)
  EVENT tokens over <rate> target <rate>                        the last hour's Claude token rate passed today's target (pm-tokens)
  EVENT tokens ok <rate>                                        back under the target (once)
  EVENT check still <worktree> <step> <minutes>m                a pm-check step has run for an hour (again every hour)
  EVENT orphans <worktree> <n> <cpu>% <name>×<k>,… pids=<pid>,… [pane=<pane>]
                                                                a worktree holds orphaned processes (parent a reaper) on two looks 60 s apart; a worktree is looked at when a pane of it ends a turn or is closed (_pmorphanevent); told once per set, again when a PID joins it; never what the sweep leaves out (_pmorphans)
  EVENT orphans again <worktree> …                              5 min after a line with pane=, one of its PIDs is still an orphan there (once)
Panes report with `pm-report "<line>"` (file channel .pm/run/reports.jsonl, exact and agent-independent); the
terminal is scraped only as a fallback, where a reporting line counts only when it is the pane's last reply (no
newer prompt echo below it). REVIEWED, RESET READY and WAITING lines are logged only; a turn of a reset in progress
(pm-pane reset) is logged; any other turn without a typed line is EVENT silent. Lines that cannot be delivered (PM blocked, PM pane missing, herdr down) are queued
and retried every tick. If the PM stays idle 10 min after a delivery without a state change the line is sent again
once, then a herdr notification is shown. Log: .pm/run/events.log (stderr crashes: .pm/run/watchd.log).
One daemon runs at a time: `run` holds .pm/run/watchd.lock for its life, so only it writes its state
(watchd-state.json); a second one waits up to 10 s for it (a restart's stopped daemon ending) and otherwise logs
`another pm-watchd holds watchd.lock; exiting` and exits. waiting.json and pm.json are changed only under their lock
(_pmlib.update), as pm-pane and pm-check change them (issue 504).
"""
import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
from _pmlib import (CHECKS, EVENTS, PANE_ROLES, PANES, PMINFO, ROOT, RUN, WAITING, WORKTREES, agents, check_room, cpu_pct,
                    find_key, herdr, load, log, machine_room, mem_gb, notify, now, pane_ops, pane_rss_gb, resetting, room,
                    save, transcript_ctx, update)
from _pmroute import PM as TO_PM, route
from _pmwake import Waker

PID = RUN / "watchd.pid"
LOCK = RUN / "watchd.lock"  # held by the running daemon for its whole life: one daemon writes STATE (issue 504)
LOCK_WAIT = 10  # seconds a starting daemon waits for the one a restart stopped to end
WAKE = RUN / "watchd.wake"  # this daemon's pid while it handles SIGUSR1 (_pmlib.wake_watchd reads it)
LOG = RUN / "watchd.log"
STATE = RUN / "watchd-state.json"
PM_LINES = ("STAGE READY", "UNIT READY", "ISSUE READY", "BLOCKED", "DONE")  # typed lines delivered to the pane's lead
INBOX = RUN / "inbox.jsonl"  # lines other scripts want delivered to the PM (pm-emulator-image)
LOGGED_LINES = ("REVIEWED", "RESET READY", "WAITING")  # typed lines that are logged only (pane-mode.md, Reporting lines)
REPORTED_WITHIN = 180  # seconds: a pm-report line this recent ended the turn that just ended
CTX_REARM = 50_000


def alive():
    try:
        pid = int(PID.read_text())
        os.kill(pid, 0)
        return pid
    except (FileNotFoundError, ValueError, ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
        return None


def find_pm(ags, pm):
    return next((x for x in ags if x.get("pane_id") == pm or x.get("name") == pm), None)


def send_to(name, ags_list, lines):
    """Deliver lines to a pane other than the PM (a plan, or the pane a room line is for). False: keep them queued."""
    a_ = next((x for x in ags_list if x.get("name") == name), None)
    if not a_ or a_.get("agent_status") == "blocked":
        return False
    text = " | ".join(lines)
    if herdr("agent", "prompt", name, text, check=False) is None:
        return False
    log(f"deliver to {name} " + text)
    return True


def room_tick(st, reg, checks=check_room, freed=None, given=None):
    """EVENT room for each pane in waiting.json whose limit has cleared, judged only when something freed room since
    the last look (issue 497): `freed` names it (a check ended, a pane closed or is gone, the daemon's own reading of
    memory and CPU on its timer is under the limits, the token rate went back under its target); `given` is that
    reading, used instead of measuring again. Without `freed` nothing is judged; an asker that is no longer a live
    pane is dropped. Of the panes a WAIT answer of pm-check told to wait, only the longest waiting is told, once
    `checks` finds room: the check it starts changes the room, and check_room holds the next one until the machine
    shows its load (the next timer reading judges again)."""
    waiting = load(WAITING, [])
    if not waiting:
        return []
    live = {r["name"] for r in reg}
    done, out, judged = [], [], {}
    check_told = False
    for w in waiting:
        if w.get("asker") not in live:
            done.append(w)
            continue
        if not freed:
            continue
        if "check" in w:
            if check_told:
                continue
            if "check" not in judged:
                judged["check"] = (checks(given=given) if given else checks())[0]
            if judged["check"] is None:
                out.append(f"EVENT room {w['asker']} check {w['check']}")
                done.append(w)
                check_told = True
            continue
        key = (w.get("role"), w.get("side"), w.get("issue"))
        if key not in judged:
            why = "token rate over today's target" if st.get("tokens_over") else room(*key, alive=reg, tokens=False, given=given)
            judged[key] = why
        if judged[key] is None:
            out.append(f"EVENT room {w['asker']} pane {w.get('role')} {w.get('side')}")
            done.append(w)
    if freed:
        log(f"room judged ({freed}): {len(out)} told")
    if done:
        with update(WAITING, []) as rows:  # under the lock: pm-pane or pm-check may add one at this moment (issue 504)
            rows[:] = [w for w in rows if w not in done]
    return out


def check_files():
    """The names of the heavy pm-check runs' files in CHECKS (pm-check removes its own when it ends)."""
    try:
        return sorted(f.name for f in CHECKS.glob("*.json"))
    except OSError:
        return []


def what_freed(st, live_now, checks_now):
    """(reasons, cwds) since the last look (issue 497): "a check ended" when a file of CHECKS went, "a pane closed"
    when a live registered pane ({name: cwd}) is no longer live (closed, or gone), with the cwds of those panes.
    Keeps what it saw in st["checks_seen"] and st["live_panes"]."""
    reasons = []
    if set(st.get("checks_seen") or []) - set(checks_now):
        reasons.append("a check ended")
    st["checks_seen"] = list(checks_now)
    before = st.get("live_panes") if isinstance(st.get("live_panes"), dict) else {}
    cwds = [c for n, c in before.items() if n not in live_now]
    if any(n not in live_now for n in before):
        reasons.append("a pane closed")
    st["live_panes"] = dict(live_now)
    return reasons, cwds


def turn_end(name, entry, reported_at, last, at):
    """What a registered pane's ended turn gives: (event line or None, log line or None) (issue 497). A turn ends with
    a typed line (pane-mode.md, Reporting lines): sent with pm-report within REPORTED_WITHIN seconds, or, as the
    fallback, the last reply on the screen. A line of PM_LINES is delivered, one of LOGGED_LINES logged; a turn of a
    reset in progress (pm-pane reset's `resetting`) is logged; any other turn is `EVENT silent <pane>`."""
    if at - (reported_at or 0) < REPORTED_WITHIN:
        return None, f"turn-end {name} (reported via file)"
    last = last or ""
    if last.startswith(PM_LINES):
        return f"EVENT ready {name} {last}", None
    if last.startswith(LOGGED_LINES):
        return None, f"turn-end {name} {last}"
    if resetting(entry, at):
        return None, f"turn-end {name} (reset)"
    return f"EVENT silent {name}", None


PANE_NAME = re.compile(r"i\d+-(?:" + "|".join(re.escape(r) for r in PANE_ROLES) + r")(?:-\S+)?")


def ours(cwd, root=ROOT):
    """True when an agent's cwd is the main checkout or a worktree beside it (<root>-<…>)."""
    if not isinstance(cwd, str) or not cwd:
        return False
    real, root = os.path.realpath(cwd), os.path.realpath(str(root))
    return real == root or real.startswith(root + "-") or real.startswith(root + os.sep)


def look():
    """(the names pm-pane opens or closes now, herdr's agent list or None, the registry), read back to back (issue 510):
    the marks, herdr's list, the registry, the marks again; a name marked at either read counts as marked. pm-pane
    sets a mark before it changes the registry and keeps it until the registry holds the new entry (new) or herdr
    lists no agent in the closed pane (close), so an agent listed by the first reads and missing from the registry is
    marked at one of the two reads unless the whole open or close fell between them."""
    ops = pane_ops()
    ags = agents()
    if ags is None:
        return ops, None, []
    reg = load(PANES, [])
    return ops | pane_ops(), ags, reg


def unregistered(ags, reg, ops, told, root=ROOT):
    """EVENT unregistered <name> <pane id> for each agent herdr holds under a pane's name (i<n>-<role>[-<unit>]) in this
    checkout or a worktree of it that no live registry entry holds in that pane, and that no pm-pane opens or closes
    now (`ops`, _pmlib.pane_ops, read before `ags` and after `reg` by look()) (issues 504, 510). `told` ({name: pane
    id}, the daemon's state) keeps each told once per pane; a name registered or gone since is forgotten, so a later
    loss is told again."""
    held = {(r.get("name"), r.get("pane_id")) for r in reg if not r.get("gone")}
    out, now_missing = [], {}
    for x in ags:
        name, pane = x.get("name"), x.get("pane_id")
        if not isinstance(name, str) or not PANE_NAME.fullmatch(name) or not ours(x.get("cwd"), root):
            continue
        if (name, pane) in held or name in ops:
            continue
        now_missing[name] = pane
        if told.get(name) != pane:
            out.append(f"EVENT unregistered {name} {pane}")
    told.clear()
    told.update(now_missing)
    return out


def deliver(pm_a, lines, st):
    """Send the lines as one prompt; on failure keep them in st['queue'] for the next tick."""
    text = " | ".join(lines)
    if not pm_a:
        # log once per episode, notify every 10 min while the queue waits (a single notification was missed on 11-10)
        if st.get("queue") != lines:
            log("queued (no PM) " + text)
        st["queue"] = lines
        if time.time() - st.get("notified_no_pm_at", 0) > 600:
            notify("pm-watchd", f"PM pane {st.get('pm_target', '')} not found; {len(lines)} event(s) queued. Run pm-watchd start --pm <pane-id>")
            st["notified_no_pm_at"] = time.time()
        return
    st["notified_no_pm_at"] = 0
    if pm_a.get("agent_status") == "blocked":
        st["queue"] = lines
        log("queued (PM blocked) " + text)
        return
    r = herdr("agent", "prompt", pm_a.get("name") or pm_a.get("pane_id"), text, check=False)
    if r is None:
        st["queue"] = lines
        log("queued (prompt failed) " + text)
        return
    st["queue"] = []
    log("deliver " + text)
    st["pending"] = dict(text=text, at=time.time(), pm_seq=pm_a.get("state_change_seq"), resent=0)


# Terminal grammar of the two agents (fallback path; the primary channel is pm-report -> reports.jsonl):
#   Claude Code: reply rows start with ⏺ at column 0 and continue indented; prompt echo ❯ text; tool results ⎿ …
#   Codex:       reply rows start with • at column 0 and continue indented; prompt echo › text (the empty box reads
#                "› Ask Codex to do anything"); tool calls are • Ran/Explored/… rows whose results start with └
REPLY_BULLETS = ("⏺", "•")
ECHO_BULLETS = ("❯", "›")
TOOL_RESULT = ("⎿", "└")
CODEX_TOOL_WORDS = ("Ran ", "Explored", "Read ", "Edited", "Searched", "Worked for", "Thinking")
ECHO_PLACEHOLDER = "Ask Codex to do anything"


def report_line(raw, allow_indented=False):
    """The reporting line in one terminal row, or None. Indented rows count only when the caller has confirmed they
    belong to a reply, so a file printed by a tool that contains a reporting line is not a report."""
    if raw[:1].isspace() and not allow_indented:
        return None
    s = raw.strip()
    if not s or s.startswith(ECHO_BULLETS + TOOL_RESULT):
        return None
    s = re.sub(r"^[^A-Za-z]+", "", s)
    return s if s.startswith(PM_LINES + LOGGED_LINES) else None


def last_report_line(name):
    """The reporting line of the pane's latest reply. Scanning upward from the input box, a prompt echo means
    everything above it belongs to an earlier turn, so the result is '' then. An indented candidate row is kept
    until the block it belongs to is known: a reply bullet above it adopts it, a tool row drops it."""
    tail = herdr("agent", "read", name, "--source", "recent-unwrapped", "--lines", "200", check=False) or {}
    txt = tail.get("text") or tail.get("output") or tail.get("raw") or ""
    if isinstance(txt, list):
        txt = "\n".join(map(str, txt))
    pending = None
    for row in reversed(str(txt).splitlines()):
        s = row.strip()
        if s.startswith(ECHO_BULLETS):
            body = s[1:].strip()
            if body and body != ECHO_PLACEHOLDER:
                return ""
            continue
        if s.startswith(REPLY_BULLETS) and not row[:1].isspace():
            body = s[1:].strip()
            if body.startswith(CODEX_TOOL_WORDS):  # a Codex tool call row, not a reply
                pending = None
                continue
            r = report_line(row)
            return r or pending or ""
        if s.startswith(TOOL_RESULT):
            pending = None
            continue
        if row[:1].isspace():
            if pending is None:
                pending = report_line(row, allow_indented=True)
            continue
        r = report_line(row)
        if r:
            return r
    return pending or ""


REPORTS = RUN / "reports.jsonl"


def file_reports(st):
    """New lines panes wrote with pm-report since the last tick: [(pane, line)]. Offset kept in st['reports_pos']."""
    if not REPORTS.exists():
        return []
    pos = st.get("reports_pos", 0)
    size = REPORTS.stat().st_size
    if size < pos:  # rotated or truncated
        pos = 0
    out = []
    with REPORTS.open("rb") as f:
        f.seek(pos)
        chunk = f.read()
    for line in chunk.decode(errors="replace").splitlines():
        try:
            o = json.loads(line)
            out.append((o["pane"], o["line"]))
        except (ValueError, KeyError):
            continue
    st["reports_pos"] = pos + len(chunk)
    return out


def inbox_lines(st):
    """New EVENT lines appended to inbox.jsonl since the last tick. Offset kept in st['inbox_pos']."""
    if not INBOX.exists():
        return []
    pos = st.get("inbox_pos", 0)
    if INBOX.stat().st_size < pos:
        pos = 0
    with INBOX.open("rb") as f:
        f.seek(pos)
        chunk = f.read()
    out = []
    for line in chunk.decode(errors="replace").splitlines():
        try:
            out.append(json.loads(line)["line"])
        except (ValueError, KeyError):
            continue
    st["inbox_pos"] = pos + len(chunk)
    return out


def top_panes(reg, n=2):
    rows = []
    for r in reg:
        try:
            rows.append((pane_rss_gb(r["pane_id"]), r["name"]))
        except Exception:
            pass
    rows.sort(reverse=True)
    return ",".join(f"{name} {gb:.1f}GB" for gb, name in rows[:n])


def check_ctx(prev, session, limit, label):
    """Append an EVENT ctx when the session's transcript context passed the limit; re-arms every CTX_REARM tokens."""
    if not session:
        return None
    if session != prev.get("ctx_session"):
        prev.update(ctx_session=session, ctx_reported_at=0, ctx_mtime=None, ctx_checked=0)
    if time.time() - prev.get("ctx_checked", 0) < 60:
        return None
    prev["ctx_checked"] = time.time()
    ctx, mtime = transcript_ctx(session)
    if not mtime or mtime == prev.get("ctx_mtime"):
        return None
    prev["ctx_mtime"] = mtime
    if ctx and ctx > limit and ctx >= prev.get("ctx_reported_at", 0) + CTX_REARM:
        prev["ctx_reported_at"] = ctx
        return f"EVENT ctx {label} {ctx // 1000}K"
    return None


def hold_lock(wait=LOCK_WAIT):
    """The open lock file, held for the daemon's life, or None when another daemon still holds it after `wait`."""
    import fcntl
    f = open(LOCK, "a")
    end = time.time() + wait
    while True:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            return f
        except OSError:
            if time.time() >= end:
                f.close()
                return None
            time.sleep(0.2)


def run(a):
    pm = a.pm
    st = load(STATE, {"seen": {}, "last_mem": 0, "pending": None, "queue": [], "pm": {}})
    st.setdefault("queue", []); st.setdefault("pm", {}); st["pm_target"] = pm
    waker = Waker()
    waker.install_signal()
    WAKE.write_text(str(os.getpid()))
    socket_state, watch_ids = None, set()
    while True:
        try:
            ops, ags_list, reg_now = look()
            if ags_list is None:  # herdr did not answer: no judgement this tick
                log("herdr agent list failed; tick skipped")
                waker.close()
                waker.wait(a.interval)
                continue
            ags = {x.get("pane_id"): x for x in ags_list}
            pm_a = find_pm(ags_list, pm)
            events = list(st.get("queue") or [])
            reg = [r for r in reg_now if not r.get("gone")]
            watch_ids = {r["pane_id"] for r in reg} | ({pm_a["pane_id"]} if pm_a else set())
            from _pmquota import tick as quota_tick
            events.extend(quota_tick(ags_list))
            from _pmstill import tick as still_tick
            events.extend(still_tick(st))
            from _pmorphanevent import due_for, tick as orphan_tick
            # what frees room (issue 497): a heavy check ended, a registered pane closed or is gone
            given, at = None, time.time()
            freed, left = what_freed(st, {r["name"]: r.get("cwd") for r in reg if r.get("pane_id") in ags}, check_files())
            if left:
                due_for(st, left, at)  # a closed pane's worktree: its orphans are looked for now and 60 s later
            seen = st["seen"]
            # primary channel: lines the panes reported through pm-report (exact, agent-independent)
            events.extend(inbox_lines(st))
            for pane, line in file_reports(st):
                seen.setdefault(pane, {})["reported_at"] = time.time()
                if line.startswith(PM_LINES):
                    events.append(f"EVENT ready {pane} {line}")
                else:
                    log(f"report {pane} {line}")
            for r in reg:
                name, pid = r["name"], r["pane_id"]
                prev = seen.get(name, {})
                if prev.get("pane_id") not in (None, pid):  # reopened in another pane: forget the old history
                    prev = {}
                a_ = ags.get(pid)
                if not a_:
                    if not prev.get("gone"):
                        events.append(f"EVENT gone {name}")
                    seen[name] = {**prev, "pane_id": pid, "gone": True}
                    continue
                status, seq, cseq = a_.get("agent_status"), a_.get("state_change_seq"), a_.get("completion_seq") or 0
                finished = status in ("idle", "done") and (prev.get("status") == "working" or (prev and cseq > (prev.get("cseq") or 0)))
                if finished:
                    t_end = time.time()
                    reported = t_end - prev.get("reported_at", 0) < REPORTED_WITHIN
                    e, line = turn_end(name, r, prev.get("reported_at", 0), "" if reported else last_report_line(name), t_end)
                    if e:
                        events.append(e)
                    if line:
                        log(line)
                    due_for(st, [r.get("cwd")], t_end)  # the pane's worktree: its orphans now and 60 s later
                if status == "blocked" and prev.get("status") != "blocked":
                    events.append(f"EVENT blocked {name}")
                if status == "working":
                    if prev.get("status") == "working" and prev.get("seq") == seq:
                        if time.time() - prev.get("since", time.time()) > a.stale_hours * 3600 and not prev.get("stale"):
                            events.append(f"EVENT stale {name} {a.stale_hours}h")
                            prev["stale"] = True
                    else:
                        prev = {**prev, "since": time.time(), "stale": False}
                e = check_ctx(prev, (a_.get("agent_session") or {}).get("value") or r.get("session"), a.ctx, name)
                if e:
                    events.append(e)
                seen[name] = {**prev, "pane_id": pid, "status": status, "seq": seq, "cseq": cseq, "gone": False}
            if pm_a:
                e = check_ctx(st["pm"], (pm_a.get("agent_session") or {}).get("value"), a.pm_ctx, "pm")
                if e:
                    events.append(e)
            used, su, stot = mem_gb()
            if used > a.mem:
                if time.time() - st.get("last_mem", 0) > 600:
                    events.append(f"EVENT mem {used:.1f}GB swap {su:.1f}/{stot:.1f}GB top={top_panes(reg)}")
                    st["last_mem"] = time.time()
                    st["mem_over"] = True
            elif st.get("mem_over") and used < a.mem - 1.0:  # back under budget with 1 GB to spare: tell the PM once
                events.append(f"EVENT mem ok {used:.1f}GB")
                st["mem_over"] = False
            if time.time() - st.get("cpu_checked", 0) >= 30:  # a second of measuring, so not on every wake-up
                st["cpu_checked"] = time.time()
                cpu = cpu_pct()
                if cpu is not None and cpu > a.cpu:
                    st["cpu_streak"] = st.get("cpu_streak", 0) + 1
                    if st["cpu_streak"] >= 3 and time.time() - st.get("last_cpu", 0) > 600:
                        events.append(f"EVENT cpu {cpu:.0f}% top={top_panes(reg)}")
                        st["last_cpu"] = time.time()
                        st["cpu_over"] = True
                elif cpu is not None:
                    st["cpu_streak"] = 0
                    if st.get("cpu_over") and cpu < a.cpu - 10:
                        events.append(f"EVENT cpu ok {cpu:.0f}%")
                        st["cpu_over"] = False
                # the timer's reading of memory and CPU judges room too, with no look of its own (issue 497)
                reading = {"mem": (used, su, stot), "cpu": cpu}
                if load(WAITING, []) and machine_room(given=reading) is None:
                    freed.append("the machine is under its limits")
                    given = reading
            if time.time() - st.get("tokens_checked", 0) > 300:  # transcripts are large: look every 5 minutes
                st["tokens_checked"] = time.time()
                from _pmtokens import fmt, status as token_status
                rate, tgt, over = token_status()
                if over and not st.get("tokens_over"):
                    events.append(f"EVENT tokens over {fmt(tgt, rate)} target {fmt(tgt, tgt['per_hour'])}")
                    st["tokens_over"] = True
                elif st.get("tokens_over") and not over:
                    events.append(f"EVENT tokens ok {fmt(tgt, rate)}" if tgt else "EVENT tokens ok (no target)")
                    st["tokens_over"] = False
                    freed.append("the token rate is under its target")
            events.extend(orphan_tick(st))
            # a pane herdr holds that the registry does not (issue 504): judged on every look, which herdr's pane events
            # (pane.created, pane.agent_detected) and the end of a pm-pane new or close (its wake) bring
            events.extend(unregistered(ags_list, reg_now, ops, st.setdefault("unregistered", {})))
            events.extend(room_tick(st, reg, freed=", ".join(freed), given=given))
            if events:
                for e in events:
                    if e not in (st.get("queue") or []):
                        log(e)
                full_reg, wts = load(PANES, []), load(WORKTREES, [])
                to_pm, others = [], {}
                for e in events:
                    target = route(e, full_reg, wts)
                    if target == "":
                        log("dropped (its pane is gone) " + e)
                    elif target is TO_PM:
                        to_pm.append(e)
                    else:
                        others.setdefault(target, []).append(e)
                stuck = [e for name, lines in others.items() if not send_to(name, ags_list, lines) for e in lines]
                if to_pm:
                    deliver(pm_a, to_pm, st)
                else:
                    st["queue"] = []
                st["queue"] = list(st.get("queue") or []) + stuck
            # PM responsiveness: a working PM consumes queued prompts inside its turn; only an idle PM with no
            # state change since the delivery gets the line again.
            pend = st.get("pending")
            if pend:
                if pm_a and (pm_a.get("agent_status") == "working" or pm_a.get("state_change_seq") != pend.get("pm_seq")):
                    st["pending"] = None
                elif time.time() - pend["at"] > 600:
                    if pend["resent"] == 0 and pm_a:
                        herdr("agent", "prompt", pm_a.get("name") or pm_a.get("pane_id"), pend["text"], check=False)
                        pend.update(at=time.time(), resent=1)
                        log("re-deliver " + pend["text"])
                    else:
                        notify("EmuForge PM unresponsive", pend["text"][:120])
                        log("PM unresponsive; notified user")
                        st["pending"] = None
            save(STATE, st)
        except Exception as e:  # keep the daemon alive
            log(f"watchd error {e!r}")
        on = waker.watch(watch_ids)
        if on != socket_state:
            log("herdr event socket in use" if on else f"herdr event socket unavailable ({waker.error}); looking every {a.interval}s")
            socket_state = on
        # while the CPU is being watched for a streak, look again in 30 s even when nothing happens; a worktree due for
        # an orphan look (_pmorphanevent) wakes the daemon at its time
        timeout = min(a.interval, 30) if st.get("cpu_streak") else a.interval
        try:
            from _pmorphanevent import next_look
            due_at = next_look(st)
        except Exception:
            due_at = None
        if due_at is not None:
            timeout = max(1, min(timeout, due_at - time.time()))
        waker.wait(timeout)


def ancestors():
    pids, pid = set(), os.getpid()
    for _ in range(40):
        out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "ppid=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
        if not out or not out.isdigit() or int(out) <= 1:
            break
        pid = int(out)
        pids.add(pid)
    return pids


def detect_pm_pane(ags, env_pane):
    """The pane this command runs in, without trusting the environment: Codex runs shell commands inside a long-lived
    app-server whose HERDR_PANE_ID froze when it started (on 2026-11-10 it pointed at a pane closed a week before).
    1) a live pane whose shell is an ancestor of this process (Claude PM);
    2) the only unregistered agent in this folder that is working right now (Codex PM: it is running this command);
    3) the environment's pane if it exists. Returns (pane_id, how) or (None, candidates)."""
    plist = (herdr("pane", "list", check=False) or {}).get("panes", [])
    live = {p["pane_id"] for p in plist}
    anc = ancestors()
    for p in plist:
        info = herdr("pane", "process-info", "--pane", p["pane_id"], check=False) or {}
        shell = (find_key(info, "process_info") or {}).get("shell_pid") if isinstance(find_key(info, "process_info"), dict) else None
        if shell and shell in anc:
            return p["pane_id"], "process tree"
    registered = {r["name"] for r in load(PANES, [])}
    working = [x for x in ags if x.get("agent_status") == "working" and x.get("name") not in registered
               and str(x.get("cwd", "")).rstrip("/") == str(ROOT)]
    if len(working) == 1:
        return working[0]["pane_id"], "the one working agent here"
    if env_pane in live:
        return env_pane, "environment"
    cands = [f"{x.get('pane_id')} ({x.get('name') or x.get('agent')}, {x.get('agent_status')})" for x in ags if str(x.get("cwd", "")).rstrip("/") == str(ROOT)]
    return None, cands


def stop():
    pid = alive()
    if pid:
        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)
        PID.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        WAKE.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    return pid


def main():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    p.add_argument("cmd", choices=["start", "stop", "status", "tail", "run", "whoami"])
    p.add_argument("n", nargs="?", default="30")
    p.add_argument("--pm"); p.add_argument("--interval", type=int, default=60); p.add_argument("--mem", type=float, default=22.5)
    p.add_argument("--cpu", type=float, default=90)
    p.add_argument("--ctx", type=int, default=300000); p.add_argument("--pm-ctx", type=int, default=1000000); p.add_argument("--stale-hours", type=float, default=3)
    a = p.parse_args()
    if a.cmd in ("start", "stop"):
        from _pmlib import guard
        guard(f"pm-watchd {a.cmd}")  # the pm's alone (issue 478)
    if a.cmd == "status":
        pid = alive()
        print(f"running pid {pid}" if pid else "not running", load(PMINFO, {}))
        return
    if a.cmd == "tail":
        n = int(a.n)
        lines = EVENTS.read_text().splitlines()[-n:] if EVENTS.exists() else []
        print("\n".join(lines))
        err = LOG.read_text()[-1500:] if LOG.exists() else ""
        if err.strip():
            print("--- watchd.log (stderr) ---\n" + err)
        return
    if a.cmd == "stop":
        pid = stop()
        print(f"stopped {pid}" if pid else "not running")
        return
    if a.cmd == "run":
        lock = hold_lock()
        if lock is None:
            log(f"another pm-watchd holds watchd.lock; exiting (pid {os.getpid()})")
            sys.exit(1)
        PID.write_text(str(os.getpid()))
        log(f"watchd run pid={os.getpid()} pm={a.pm}")
        run(a)
        return
    # start / whoami: find the PM pane without trusting HERDR_PANE_ID (see detect_pm_pane)
    ags_now = agents() or []
    if a.pm:
        pm_pane, how = (find_pm(ags_now, a.pm) or {}).get("pane_id", a.pm), "--pm"
        if pm_pane not in {p["pane_id"] for p in (herdr("pane", "list", check=False) or {}).get("panes", [])}:
            sys.exit(f"pane {pm_pane} does not exist (herdr pane list)")
    else:
        pm_pane, how = detect_pm_pane(ags_now, os.environ.get("HERDR_PANE_ID"))
        if not pm_pane:
            sys.exit(f"cannot tell which pane is the PM (env HERDR_PANE_ID={os.environ.get('HERDR_PANE_ID')} is not a live pane and no single "
                     f"working agent runs in this folder). Run: pm-watchd start --pm <pane-id>. Candidates: {', '.join(how) or 'none'}")
    if a.cmd == "whoami":
        print(f"{pm_pane} (by {how})")
        return
    pm_a = find_pm(ags_now, pm_pane) or {}
    if not pm_a:
        print(f"note: no agent is detected in {pm_pane} yet; events will be delivered to the pane id once an agent runs there")
    pm_session = (pm_a.get("agent_session") or {}).get("value")
    old = load(PMINFO, {})
    pid = alive()
    if pid:
        stop()
        print(f"restarting: pid {pid} watched {old.get('pm_pane')}/{old.get('pm_name')}, now {pm_pane}/{pm_a.get('name')}")
        time.sleep(0.5)
    # under the lock, on pm.json as it is now: pm-pane new may add to session_issues at this moment (issue 504)
    with update(PMINFO, {}) as info:
        same = info.get("pm_pane") == pm_pane
        sessions = [s for s in info.get("pm_sessions", []) if s] if same else []
        if pm_session and pm_session not in sessions:
            sessions.append(pm_session)
        # issues per PM session (pm-pane new appends): pm-cost shares a PM session's cost between the issues it ran
        session_issues = info.get("session_issues", {}) if same else {}
        if pm_session:
            session_issues.setdefault(pm_session, [])
        info.clear()
        info.update(pm_pane=pm_pane, pm_name=pm_a.get("name"), pm_session=pm_session, pm_sessions=sessions,
                    session_issues=session_issues, workspace=pm_a.get("workspace_id") or os.environ.get("HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID"),
                    started=now())
    args = [sys.executable, "-I", os.path.abspath(__file__), "run", "--pm", pm_pane, "--interval", str(a.interval),
            "--mem", str(a.mem), "--cpu", str(a.cpu), "--ctx", str(a.ctx), "--pm-ctx", str(a.pm_ctx), "--stale-hours", str(a.stale_hours)]
    with open(LOG, "a") as out:
        proc = subprocess.Popen(args, stdout=out, stderr=out, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
    time.sleep(0.5)
    print(f"started pid {proc.pid} pm={pm_a.get('name') or pm_pane} ({pm_pane}) session={pm_session} fallback interval={a.interval}s mem>{a.mem}GB cpu>{a.cpu:.0f}% ctx>{a.ctx} pm-ctx>{a.pm_ctx}")


main()
